  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If the target creature is an illegal target when Surly Badgersaur's last ability tries to resolve, the ability doesn't resolve. If it's a legal target but Surly Badgersaur is no longer on the battlefield when the ability resolves, the target creature won't deal or be dealt damage.",
      "oracle_id": "0209dc74-ac49-4deb-907a-e9fa49d27a0f",
      "published_at": "2020-04-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you discard a card as a cost to cast a spell or activate an ability, Surly Badgersaur's triggered ability resolves before that spell or ability but after you've chosen targets for it. If you discard a card while a spell or ability is resolving, that spell or ability finishes resolving before Surly Badgersaur's triggered ability does.",
      "oracle_id": "0209dc74-ac49-4deb-907a-e9fa49d27a0f",
      "published_at": "2020-04-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Surly Badgersaur's abilities are triggered abilities, not activated abilities. They don't allow you to discard a card whenever you want; rather, you need some other way of discarding a card, such as a cycling ability.",
      "oracle_id": "0209dc74-ac49-4deb-907a-e9fa49d27a0f",
      "published_at": "2020-04-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When Rotting Rats's \"enters\" ability resolves, first the player whose turn it is chooses a card to discard, then each other player in turn order does the same, then all cards are discarded at the same time. No one sees what the other players are discarding before deciding which card to discard.",
      "oracle_id": "1f361ae9-98a2-40ff-a579-fa5b9f510df4",
      "published_at": "2009-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For Juri's second ability, use its power from when it was last on the battlefield to determine how much damage is dealt. If that power was 0 or less, Juri deals no damage.",
      "oracle_id": "3364bad6-6d0a-4141-b410-86e3d9e1916e",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Juri's first ability doesn't allow you to sacrifice any permanents. You'll have to find another way to do that.",
      "oracle_id": "3364bad6-6d0a-4141-b410-86e3d9e1916e",
      "published_at": "2020-11-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When Merchant of Venom's second ability resolves, first the player whose turn it is chooses which creature they're going to sacrifice, then each other player in turn order does the same. Players will know the choices of previous players when making their choices. Then all chosen creatures are sacrificed by their controllers simultaneously.",
      "oracle_id": "3918eaa7-5a34-4d6a-be93-a95e733d041b",
      "published_at": "2026-03-20",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Pitiless Plunderer dies at the same time as one or more other creatures you control, its ability will still trigger for each of those other creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "a784481f-eccb-4112-bb38-04a659319660",
      "published_at": "2018-01-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature has multiple evasion abilities, such as shadow and flying, a creature can block it only if that creature satisfies all of the appropriate evasion abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you cast a card this way, you may not cast it for any other alternative costs it has, but you may pay for additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the spell requires an additional cost, you must pay that cost.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If your opponent discards a card while you control Dauthi Voidwalker, abilities that function when that card is discarded still work, even though that card never reaches that player's graveyard. In addition, spells or abilities that check the characteristics of the discarded card can find that card in exile.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Playing a card with Dauthi Voidwalker's last ability is still subject to normal timing restrictions.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tokens still die while Dauthi Voidwalker is on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "While Dauthi Voidwalker is on the battlefield, nontoken creatures your opponents control won't die. They'll be exiled instead. Abilities that would trigger when those creatures die won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "f1c2dbe2-fbe0-4058-bdf1-91d1b1832786",
      "published_at": "2021-06-18",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
